lookup['1967-142.3']['reconstruction']=r"""Commutativity, the unit, completeness, continuity of the involution and restriction to continuous characters fix one explicit version of the notebook's proposed axiomatization. These choices are supplied by the editor; the notes do not uniquely determine all of them. Cylinder-measure representation is weaker than the stated Radon representation."""
lookup['1967-142.3']['present_status']=r"""As of November 2026, the opened literature supplies sufficient representation criteria in specified nuclear and moment-determinate settings, but those results do not give a characterization of the exact universal property stated here. The incomplete part is the passage from hypotheses on one functional or on a specified nuclear presentation to an algebra-level criterion quantifying over every continuous squares-positive functional. This audit does not establish that the reconstructed characterization is a generally accepted open conjecture, and the uncertainty about the notebook's intended category is retained explicitly."""
